{
  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed first floor rear extension together with changes to front fenestrations, by virtue of its design, scale, siting, dimensions and awkward relationship with the host property would give rise to a contrived and bulky form of development that would be detrimental to the visual amenities of Warwick Road and views from the rear of properties along Denton Road.  Additionally, the proposal would both unbalance and detract from the character and symmetry of the prevailing build form within the street scene. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve the character and appearance of the application dwelling and the wider setting, contrary to Policies D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy, DMD11 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed flat roofed first floor rear extension by reason of its excessive width, design, scale and siting would constitute an obtrusive and overly dominant form of development that would result in an unacceptable loss of light, outlook, and an increased sense of enclosure detrimental to the occupiers of the adjoining neighbouring property at terrace along Denton Road. In this respect, the proposal would be contrary to policy CP30 of the Core Strategy, policy DMD8 of the Development Management Document as well the NPPF (2024)."
  ],
